      "side": 1,
      "message": "No build targets, and not something at google either, https://github.com/lineage-next/android_packages_apps_Twelve\nThis app includes okhttp as a prebuilt and includes it statically as can be seen here https://github.com/lineage-next/android_packages_apps_Twelve/blob/lineage-22.0/app/libs/Android.bp#L529\nMaybe the java_import -\u003e java_library_static dance causes the problem?\n\nI see the following warnings\n```\nMissing class org.bouncycastle.jsse.BCSSLParameters (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.BouncyCastlePlatform.configureTlsExtensions(javax.net.ssl.SSLSocket, java.lang.String, java.util.List) and 1 other context)\nMissing class org.bouncycastle.jsse.BCSSLSocket (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.BouncyCastlePlatform.configureTlsExtensions(javax.net.ssl.SSLSocket, java.lang.String, java.util.List) and 5 other contexts)\nMissing class org.bouncycastle.jsse.provider.BouncyCastleJsseProvider (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.BouncyCastlePlatform.\u003cinit\u003e())\nMissing class org.conscrypt.Conscrypt$Version (referenced from: boolean okhttp3.internal.platform.ConscryptPlatform$Companion.atLeastVersion(int, int, int))\nMissing class org.conscrypt.Conscrypt (referenced from: boolean okhttp3.internal.platform.ConscryptPlatform$Companion.atLeastVersion(int, int, int) and 9 other contexts)\nMissing class org.conscrypt.ConscryptHostnameVerifier (referenced from: javax.net.ssl.X509TrustManager okhttp3.internal.platform.ConscryptPlatform.platformTrustManager() and 1 other context)\nMissing class org.openjsse.javax.net.ssl.SSLParameters (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.OpenJSSEPlatform.configureTlsExtensions(javax.net.ssl.SSLSocket, java.lang.String, java.util.List))\nMissing class org.openjsse.javax.net.ssl.SSLSocket (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.OpenJSSEPlatform.configureTlsExtensions(javax.net.ssl.SSLSocket, java.lang.String, java.util.List) and 1 other context)\nMissing class org.openjsse.net.ssl.OpenJSSE (referenced from: void okhttp3.internal.platform.OpenJSSEPlatform.\u003cinit\u003e())```\n\nManually propagating the rules via this change makes them go away (it\u0027s just dontwarn rules)\n\nIf you want to try building it just remove https://github.com/lineage-next/android_packages_apps_Twelve/blob/lineage-22.0/app/Android.bp#L13, that\u0027s hopefully a workaround I\u0027ll kill sooner than later\n\nAfter that I still have one warning caused by coil3\n`Warning: Missing class coil3.core.R$id (referenced from: coil3.request.ViewTargetRequestManager coil3.request.ViewTargetRequestManagerKt.getRequestManager(android.view.View))\n)`\nbut this is likely yet another difference in the way id resources are handled and I\u0027m not ready yet to figure that one out :)",
